      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"Inverted\" is improper here, and \"lowest order at 0xff000000\" is a contradiction in terms as by definition the lowest order byte in a 32-bit value is at 0x000000ff. Because you\u0027re referring to the bytes in an IPv4 address, I suggest something like\n\n  ...with the first byte of the address in the lowest-order bits of the int.\n\n(alongside a justification of why you find this confusing).\n\nSuggest also adding an example to help clarify. Order of data is a confusing problem, and examples are often illuminating.",
